url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","login":"AThousandShips","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips"},"body":"At minimum we should drop Windows 7 support, but Windows 8 support officially ended almost 2 years ago so I'd say the same should apply there\r\n\r\nIf people are unable to run more modern versions of Windows I'd say they are either not going to have a good time running Godot 4.x anyway, seeing how their hardware is too old to support a 10 year old OS, or they should run something that is safer like Linux that gets security updates etc. (which would be better from a performance perspective anyway)\r\n\r\nI'd say at least that we should drop official support for pre Windows 10, as we can't expect people to test on unsafe versions, or encourage it","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106959#pullrequestreview-2889220469","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106959","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-06-02T16:47:13Z"}]